1
00:00:00,081 --> 00:00:02,743
Every prediction market on DreamDEX expires —

2
00:00:02,951 --> 00:00:05,556
sixty seconds, fifteen minutes, a day.

3
00:00:05,914 --> 00:00:09,699
Liquidity you have to rebuild every window isn't liquidity.

4
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:12,419
So we built a vault that outlives the markets

5
00:00:12,431 --> 00:00:13,102
it quotes.

6
00:00:14,233 --> 00:00:15,297
This is the vault, live.

7
00:00:15,679 --> 00:00:18,827
Nine and a half thousand tUSDC of depositor capital,

8
00:00:19,221 --> 00:00:21,999
and a hundred and ninety-three quotes placed inside this

9
00:00:21,999 --> 00:00:23,098
venue's own book —

10
00:00:23,631 --> 00:00:25,772
real money, at prices it had to honour.

11
00:00:26,142 --> 00:00:27,149
Not a reading of the venue.

12
00:00:27,508 --> 00:00:28,226
A position in it.

13
00:00:29,157 --> 00:00:30,673
Which means we can be asked whether the book

14
00:00:30,673 --> 00:00:31,298
got better.

15
00:00:31,668 --> 00:00:34,839
We rebuilt seventy of the windows we've quoted, twice,

16
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,749
from the venue's own order rows —

17
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,029
once with our orders in, once with them taken

18
00:00:39,041 --> 00:00:39,330
out.

19
00:00:39,712 --> 00:00:41,923
Twenty-three percent narrower with us in it.

20
00:00:42,293 --> 00:00:45,441
Tighter on sixty-six of seventy, wider on none.

21
00:00:46,896 --> 00:00:50,079
BinaryPool has no operator gate: a bot key that

22
00:00:50,079 --> 00:00:51,468
can trade can also withdraw.

23
00:00:51,838 --> 00:00:53,725
Ours owns its own orders instead.

24
00:00:54,084 --> 00:00:56,618
The operator key picks a price and a size —

25
00:00:56,954 --> 00:00:59,026
it cannot move a token, and there is no

26
00:00:59,037 --> 00:01:00,056
function that would let it.

27
00:01:00,993 --> 00:01:03,504
A hundred and fifteen tests, nine of them against

28
00:01:03,504 --> 00:01:05,229
the real venue on a fork.

29
00:01:05,599 --> 00:01:08,840
Ninety-seven percent line coverage on the vault, and

30
00:01:08,956 --> 00:01:10,912
every one of its forty-three functions.

31
00:01:12,037 --> 00:01:14,930
A window expired at seventeen hundred UTC.

32
00:01:15,289 --> 00:01:17,199
No bot ran, nobody called anything.

33
00:01:17,569 --> 00:01:20,763
Somnia's reactivity precompile woke the vault at the

34
00:01:20,775 --> 00:01:23,275
second it was armed for, and it settled its

35
00:01:23,287 --> 00:01:23,958
own position.

36
00:01:25,185 --> 00:01:26,493
Now the uncomfortable part.

37
00:01:26,863 --> 00:01:30,081
This project once published a two point three seven

38
00:01:30,081 --> 00:01:30,833
percent return.

39
00:01:31,215 --> 00:01:33,785
That number was wrong: the ledger summed the episodes

40
00:01:33,785 --> 00:01:36,041
that closed into a complete set and dropped the

41
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:38,565
ones that went one-sided, so it could not produce

42
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:39,155
a loss.

43
00:01:39,525 --> 00:01:41,886
We found it ourselves and published the correction.

44
00:01:43,109 --> 00:01:46,546
Today, honestly: depositors are down two percent, and

45
00:01:46,558 --> 00:01:48,525
one in five filled quotes goes adverse.

46
00:01:48,919 --> 00:01:50,157
That's the real risk —

47
00:01:50,539 --> 00:01:53,328
one leg fills, the market walks away from the

48
00:01:53,328 --> 00:01:55,713
other, and the vault holds a direction worth one

49
00:01:55,713 --> 00:01:56,199
or nothing.

50
00:01:56,581 --> 00:01:59,717
Twenty-six of those, carried to settlement, averaged

51
00:01:59,729 --> 00:02:02,495
minus thirty percent, with a minus one hundred in

52
00:02:02,507 --> 00:02:02,715
them.

53
00:02:03,085 --> 00:02:05,342
So the vault stopped carrying them: it buys the

54
00:02:05,342 --> 00:02:08,143
missing side, and the pair is worth exactly one

55
00:02:08,143 --> 00:02:08,676
either way.

56
00:02:09,092 --> 00:02:12,889
Fourteen so far, averaging minus one percent, worst minus

57
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,034
three and a half.

58
00:02:15,253 --> 00:02:19,165
Sixteen reproducible defects in DreamDEX and its SDK,

59
00:02:19,662 --> 00:02:21,445
each one with a transaction hash.

60
00:02:21,815 --> 00:02:24,408
A pool freezes its whole order book the moment

61
00:02:24,408 --> 00:02:25,588
a window expires —

62
00:02:25,831 --> 00:02:28,551
including the calls the SDK documents as the way

63
00:02:28,551 --> 00:02:29,558
to get your escrow out.

64
00:02:30,577 --> 00:02:32,996
Abadi is a market maker that survives its own

65
00:02:32,996 --> 00:02:37,070
markets expiring, a vault that settles itself when nobody

66
00:02:37,082 --> 00:02:40,091
is watching, and a measurably tighter book for everyone

67
00:02:40,091 --> 00:02:40,820
else trading it.

68
00:02:41,190 --> 00:02:43,447
Every number you've seen is read from the chain —

69
00:02:43,899 --> 00:02:45,924
including the ones we'd rather not show you.
